% Generate `web/src/main.jsx`: the React entry point. It mounts `App` (from `./App.jsx`)
% into `#root` via `createRoot`, inside `<React.StrictMode>` and an in-file `ErrorBoundary`,
% and installs global browser error handlers. All crash paths funnel to
% `reportClientError` (from `./api.js`, which handles dedup/capping and never throws) so
% failures reach PostHog instead of leaving a white screen. Also imports `./styles.css`.
% The `crash-*` class names below are the contract with styles.css.

## ErrorBoundary (class component — only classes can be error boundaries)
Catches render-tree errors so the app shows a recoverable panel instead of a white screen.
State `{ crashed: false }`; `static getDerivedStateFromError()` → `{ crashed: true }`.
`componentDidCatch(error, info)` reports via
`reportClientError('react-boundary', error?.message || String(error), error?.stack, { componentStack: (info?.componentStack || '').slice(0, 2000) })`.
`render()`: when not crashed, `this.props.children`; else a `crash-screen` > `crash-card`
div with an `<h2>` "Something went wrong", a `<p>` explaining the error was reported and a
reload usually fixes it, and a "Reload OpenNolan" `<button>` calling `window.location.reload()`.

## Global handlers (for errors outside React's render tree — event handlers, async, promises)
- `window` `'error'` → `reportClientError('window.onerror', e?.message || 'error', e?.error?.stack, { filename: e?.filename, line: e?.lineno, col: e?.colno })`.
- `window` `'unhandledrejection'` → with `r = e?.reason`, `reportClientError('unhandledrejection', r?.message || String(r), r?.stack)`.

## Mount
`createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(<React.StrictMode><ErrorBoundary><App /></ErrorBoundary></React.StrictMode>)`.
